# The Underkarst's cave life (Prototypes/_WF/Caverns/Life/asclepiu.yml).

wf-recipe-cave-cap-soup = cave cap soup recipe
wf-cave-root-grabs = Pale roots close round your legs!
wf-cave-sporepuff-puff = The puffball bursts in a cloud of spores!

ent-WFCaveDropletLichen = droplet lichen
    .desc = Pale, sappy lichen that beads with water. Eat it to ease cuts and burns, or cut it up to bind on a wound.
ent-WFCaveCapMushroom = cave cap
    .desc = A pale, blind mushroom from the dark. Cook two in a big bowl with water for a soup.
ent-WFFoodSoupCaveCap = cave cap soup
    .desc = A thin, earthy soup of pale cave mushrooms.

ent-WFCaveLichenPatch = droplet lichen
    .desc = A pale lichen on the flowstone, beaded with drip water. Pick it for a healing herb; it grows back.
ent-WFCaveGraspingRoot = grasping roots
    .desc = Pale roots that hang from the ceiling and close round the legs of anything that walks under them. Cut them or struggle free.
ent-WFCavePaleReeds = pale reeds
    .desc = Bleached reeds standing in the grotto shallows. Cut the stalks for plant fibre; they grow back.
ent-WFCavePitcherPod = acid pitcher
    .desc = A pitcher plant brimming with acid that it spits at anything that comes within five metres.
ent-WFCaveAcidGlob = acid glob
    .desc = A glob of caustic pitcher juice.
ent-WFCaveCapPatch = cave caps
    .desc = A patch of pale mushrooms in the damp soil. They're good to eat, and they grow back after picking.
ent-WFCaveSporePuff = spore puffball
    .desc = A swollen green puffball. It breathes out a poisonous, mind-fogging cloud at anyone who steps close, so pick your way round it.

ent-WFMobCavePaleBat = pale cave bat
    .desc = A blind bat the colour of bone. It finds you by the sound of your feet.
ent-WFMobCaveFrog = cave frog
    .desc = A blind, translucent frog. Hop hop hop in the dark.
ent-WFMobCaveCrab = cave crab
    .desc = A chalk-white crab that has never seen the sun. It still has a claw.
ent-WFMobCaveSpider = cave spider
    .desc = A pale, eyeless spider as big as a dog. The hollows are its web.
